00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.209 align:start position:0%
diabetes is a disease caused by  excessive amounts of blood glucose this  condition known as hyperglycemia is  fatal if untreated and leads to various  symptoms such as excessive urination  fatigue weight loss and blurred vision  in order to control blood glucose levels  a hormone known as insulin is made by  the pancreas to signal cells for the  uptake of blood glucose type 1 diabetes  is caused by insufficient blood insulin  and is believed to be caused by a  variety of factors such as viral  infection from the rotavirus and measles  and genetics in 1921 dr. Frederick  Banting researched a successful way to  isolate insulin from pancreatic cells in  dogs they later began mass producing  insulin for diabetic patients from pigs  saving many whoreson insolent and human  insulin only differed by one amino acid  residue at the c-terminus  in which the alanine in pig insulin is  replaced with a threonine in human  insulin because of this this meant that  pig insulin was compatible with human  insulin receptors while animal  influenced are still sometimes used  today they must be very pure as there  are impurities that have been shown to  cause allergic reactions in 1926  scientists first crystallized insulin  and then in 1955 a breakthrough by  Frederick Sanger allowed scientists to  sequence the DNA coding for insulin the  3d structure was solved by Dorothy  Hodgkin in 1969 through the use of x-ray  crystallography after Sanger's work  scientists could use this genetic code  to synthesize their own insulin  efficient mass production of insulin  began in 1978 through recombinant  bacteria in which insulin genes were  inserted for bacteria to transcribe and  translate into insulin thus the insulin  that you used is mass produced by lab  bacteria for more information on type 1  diabetes and diabetes treatment and  management please visit the protein  databank website thanks for watching
 

